    "problem_statement": "Parser peek method returns incorrect substring\n\nDescription\n\nThe `peek` method in the parser's `Reader` class is returning one character less than expected. When peeking ahead in the string, it's cutting off the last character due to an off-by-one error in the slice operation.\n\nSteps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom dotenv.parser import Reader\n\n# Create a simple reader with some content\nreader = Reader(\"hello world\")\n\n# Try to peek at the first 5 characters\nresult = reader.peek(5)\nprint(f\"Expected: 'hello', Got: '{result}'\")\n\n# Try to peek at different lengths\nprint(f\"peek(1): '{reader.peek(1)}'\")  # Should be 'h'\nprint(f\"peek(3): '{reader.peek(3)}'\")  # Should be 'hel'\n```\n\nThis affects parsing of .env files where the parser needs to look ahead to determine token boundaries and handle quoted strings properly."
  }
